{{#if tasks}}
## Tasks

You have access to a task list on the `tasks` object. Use `tasks.addTask` to add
work, `tasks.updateTask` to update a task's data, `tasks.completeTask` to mark a
task as completed, and `tasks.removeTask` to drop a task. At most
{{tasks.maxTasks}} may be recorded.

Tasks are required to form a directed acyclic graph. You may record task
dependencies when adding a task or with `tasks.setBlockedBy`. Cycles will be
automatically rejected.
{{/if}}

{{#if subagents}}
## Subagents

Use `agents.spawnSubagent` to delegate work to another agent. You have the
following agents available to you:

{{#each spawnableAgents}}
- `{{name}}`{{#if description}}: {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}

Choose the agent whose purpose best fits the work. You may only spawn the
agents listed above.
{{/if}}

{{#if board}}
## Project management

You have access to a shared project board, reached through the `project` object,
that you and other agents may use. This board is shared across the entire run.

Use epics to group related issues. Epics are used exclusively for organizational
purposes and can be created using `project.createEpic`. Issues represent units
of work to be completed and are created using `project.createIssue`, which
returns the ID of the created issue. All issues are handled in isolated
worktrees.

Issues may have dependencies configured. Submitting an issue will cause an agent
to be dispatched to handle the issue once all dependencies have been completed
(or immediately, if it has no dependencies). Each issue is worked in its own
isolated copy of the workspace, which is merged back once the issue is accepted.

You may assign an issue to any of the following agents:

{{#each board.issueAgents}}
- `{{name}}`{{#if description}}: {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}

Use `project.waitForIssue` to suspend until the issue you specify has been
completed and merged into the main worktree.

{{#if board.reviewerAgents}}
{{#if board.reviewersRequired}}
Every issue must name one or more `reviewers`.
{{else}}
An issue may name one or more `reviewers`.
{{/if}} You may name any of the following agents as a reviewer:

{{#each board.reviewerAgents}}
- `{{name}}`{{#if description}}: {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

